Improved scheduling question I would use instead of “which activities depend on which, and which can run at the same time?”:

**“At the instant doors are called, what must have *finished*, not merely started, on each shared resource, and what two or more departments must produce complete readiness at the same moment without blocking the stage, dock, desk, PA, monitor world, or green room?”**

This exposes hidden dependencies the text implies but does not spell out:

- `backline-up` is not only “after the second truck”; it also needs the stage to be free from rigging, so it must wait for `rig-bars`.
- `soundcheck` is not only “after house and wedges are rung out”; it also needs the band backline to be physically up on stage, so it must wait for `backline-up` as well.
- `clean-house` should start when the band *goes to* dinner, not when dinner ends; the source says “after the band go to dinner,” so the trigger uses `band-dinner` `event: "start"`.
- `doors-walk-up` must not start until both house cleaning and cue-build are complete; cue-build is a lighting dependency not explicitly tied to doors, but doors/show cannot happen with an unfinished lighting plot.
- `show` must wait for both the full band dinner block and the doors walk-up block, so the band is done with the green room and the room is filled.
- `strike-rig` must wait for the show to end, and because it is in the lighting track it is also explicitly gated after cue-build so the same lighting line of work cannot overlap itself.
- `backline-out` waits for the original dock-clearing step and for the show to be down plus 15 minutes.

No additional timed activity is needed; the hidden constraints are better expressed as compound readiness gates rather than invented work steps. The Rhylthyme validator/analyze/visualize tools are not available in this offline turn, so there is no live URL or Gantt here; the program below is the self-built version.

